# CONSULT-64 — Cell-to-cell visibility predicate byte-map

Mechanism analysis only. All evidence-pack facts treated as locked.

---

## Architecture: two layers

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| **Engine (sharedObject portal + clientGraphics)** | Builds portal geometry/planes, resolves object/camera **containing cell**, registers dPVS cells/portals, feeds `DPVS::Camera` each frame |
| **dPVS (vendored `src/external/3rd/library/dpvs/`)** | Performs portal backface cull, screen-rectangle clip, frustum shrink through portals, cell graph traversal → `INSTANCE_*` callbacks → draw submission |

RenderDoc locked fact: missing geometry = **whole cells never reach the renderer**. The gates below are upstream of any API draw call.

---

## 1. Portal geometry & plane construction

### 1.1 Asset load → triangle fan + winding flag

```176:180:src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/PortalPropertyTemplate.cpp
IndexedTriangleList * PortalPropertyTemplateNamespace::createPortalGeometry(PortalPropertyTemplate::VertexList const & vertices)
{
	IndexedTriangleList * const indexedTriangleList = new IndexedTriangleList;
	indexedTriangleList->addTriangleFan(&vertices[0], static_cast<int>(vertices.size()));
```

- **Winding**: per-portal `m_geometryWindingClockwise` read from IFF (`load_0001`…`load_0005`, e.g. `:334`, `:350`, `:401`).
- **Scale**: `scalePortalVertices()` at `:185–209` — default `portalScale = 1.1f` (`ConfigSharedObject.cpp:56`, getter `:78–80`). Expands portal quad radially from centroid; **no plane epsilon**.

### 1.2 Template plane equation (normal direction)

```413:421:src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/PortalPropertyTemplate.cpp
void PortalPropertyTemplateCellPortal::computePlaneEquation()
{
	...
	Vector const & v0 = vertices[indices[0]];
	Vector const & v1 = vertices[m_geometryWindingClockwise ? indices[1] : indices[2]];
	Vector const & v2 = vertices[m_geometryWindingClockwise ? indices[2] : indices[1]];
	m_plane.set(v0, v1, v2);
}
```

- **Winding swaps v1/v2** → flips normal. Used for door frame alignment (`getDoorTransform`, `:426–451`), not directly in dPVS.
- **Debug coplanarity only**: `validateCoplanar()` warns if vertex > **0.001f** from plane (`:168–169`); **Release has no runtime coplanarity gate**.

### 1.3 Runtime portal mesh → dPVS model

```686:711:src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/RenderWorld.cpp
DPVS::MeshModel *dpvsPortalModel = RenderWorld::fetchMeshModel(portalGeometry, portal->isGeometryWindingOrderClockwise());
dpvsPortalModel->set(DPVS::Model::BACKFACE_CULLABLE, true);
...
dpvsPortal = DPVS::PhysicalPortal::create(dpvsPortalModel, dpvsTargetCell);
```

- Same `IndexedTriangleList` + same clockwise flag as engine collision tests.
- Portal attached to **building object** (`Portal.cpp:394` → `m_relativeToObject->addDpvsObject`); object-to-cell matrix set in `inWorldAddDpvsObject` (`RenderWorld.cpp:648–653`) from `object->getTransform_o2c()`.

**Degenerate cases**

| Case | Mechanism | Observed failure |
|------|-----------|------------------|
| Non-coplanar asset verts | dPVS planar model derived from mesh; engine debug warns only | Intermittent BF cull / rectangle clip inconsistency; tiny view change shifts projected hull |
| `portalScale` 1.1 | Engine penetration/overlap tests use scaled verts; dPVS uses same scaled mesh | Usually *helps* grazing hits; mismatch only if scale config diverges |
| Winding asset error | BF cull uses plane from mesh; `collide()` reverses ray for CCW (`Portal.cpp:200–202`) | Portal always BF-culled from one side → **entire target cell never traversed** → sky/world shows through doorway |
| Disabled portal | `PhysicalPortal::create(model, NULL)` (`RenderWorld.cpp:697–700`) | Target cell unreachable via that portal — permanent hole (not intermittent unless `isDisabled()` debug override) |

---

## 2. Engine geometric predicates (collision / containment path)

These do **not** gate dPVS directly except where they set **`Object::m_parentCell`**.

### 2.1 Portal ray penetration (segment × mesh)

```195:209:src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/Portal.cpp
bool Portal::testPenetration(const Vector &begin, const Vector &end, float &t) const
{
	if (isGeometryWindingOrderClockwise() && getGeometry().collide(begin, end, result)) ...
	else if (!isGeometryWindingOrderClockwise() && getGeometry().collide(end, begin, result)) ...
```

Core predicate in `IndexedTriangleList::collide` (`IndexedTriangleList.cpp:353–395`):

```374:391:src/engine/shared/library/sharedMath/src/shared/IndexedTriangleList.cpp
normal = (v0 - v2).cross(v1 - v0);
if (direction.dot(normal) < std::numeric_limits<float>::min())  // backface reject
{
	plane.set(normal, v0);
	if (plane.findDirectedIntersection(start, shortenedEnd, intersection) &&
	    (start.magnitudeBetweenSquared(intersection) < ...) &&
	    intersection.inPolygon(v0, v1, v2))
```

**Plane test** — `Plane::findDirectedIntersection` (`Plane.cpp:237–244`):

```242:244:src/engine/shared/library/sharedMath/src/shared/Plane.cpp
// t0 on front (>=0), t1 on back (<=0)
if (t0 < CONST_REAL(0) || t1 > CONST_REAL(0))
	return false;
```

**Epsilons: effectively zero.** Strict `<` / `>`; on-plane (`t0==0` or `t1==0`) **passes**. No tolerance band.

**Polygon containment** — `Vector::inPolygon` (`Vector.cpp:253–256`): three cross-product same-side tests; point must lie on portal plane (comment `:262`).

**Degenerate cases**

| Case | Result | Visual |
|------|--------|--------|
| Camera/player motion segment parallel to portal plane | `direction·normal ≈ 0` → face skipped | **Player cell not updated** at doorway; dPVS still uses old cell |
| Both endpoints on plane | `t0==t1==0` → intersection at endpoint (`Plane.cpp:246–249`) | Ambiguous crossing; may or may not fire `setParentCell` |
| Grazing edge of portal quad | `inPolygon` false | No cell transition while visually “in doorway” |
| CCW portal + wrong ray direction | Only reversed ray tested | One-way crossing failure |

### 2.2 Portal sphere overlap

```214:242:src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/Portal.cpp
Plane3d const plane(v0, v1, v2);
if (Overlap3d::TestSpherePoly(sphere, vertexList, plane))
```

```469:475:src/engine/shared/library/sharedCollision/src/shared/core/Overlap3d.cpp
if(!TestSpherePlane(A,P)) return false;  // |dist| <= radius, no epsilon
...
return dist2 < (A.getRadius() * A.getRadius());  // strict <
```

Used by `CellProperty::getDestinationCells` (`CellProperty.cpp:811–858`) — **not** the render/dPVS path.

### 2.3 Cell portal crossing loop (player cell assignment)

```115:185:src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/portal/CellProperty.cpp
// Lift segment 0.1m along object up (feet → portal center heuristic)
objUpW *= 0.1f;
start += objUpW; end += objUpW;
...
CellProperty *nextCell = currentCell->getDestinationCell(cellStart, cellEnd, time);
...
if (targetCell) { object.setParentCell(targetCell); return false; }
```

`getDestinationCell` (`CellProperty.cpp:720–769`):

- **`passableOnly` default `true`** → skips `!portal->isPassable()` (`:744–745`).
- **Transform branch**: attached exterior portals transform segment world→portal-object space (`:750–754`); interior portals test in cell space (`:758`).
- **Closest portal**: `penetrated && t <= closestPortalT` (`:761–764`) — **no epsilon**; ties favor later portal in list order.
- **Stop conditions**: `time==1.0f`, `nextCell==NULL`, `nextCell==currentCell`, `nextCell==lastCell` (`:164–168`).

**Hysteresis / caching: none.** Each position notification recomputes from segment; no sticky cell, no frame cache. Early-out if same cell (`Object::setParentCell` `:1391–1393`).

**Who uses this**: player (`GroundScene.cpp:954,1054` — `addPortalCrossingNotification`), projectiles, WorldSnapshot objects. **Not** the chase camera’s authoritative cell (see §3).

### 2.4 POB floor-based `findContainingCell` (login/placement only)

Two variants:

- `PortalProperty::findContainingCell(buildingPos, …)` (`PortalProperty.cpp:344–406`) — closest floor point, `y = max(floorY, testY)`.
- `PortalProperty::findContainingCell(position_l)` (`PortalProperty.cpp:666–712`) — starts **`CellProperty::getWorldCellProperty()`** (`:668`), picks closest floor, optionally recurses nested POB.

**Not called per render frame** for camera/player at cantina. Relevant post-zone-in for **object placement**, not dPVS query cell.

### 2.5 `Object::getParentCell()` — world-cell fallback

```1372:1382:src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/object/Object.cpp
for (Object *o = getAttachedTo(); o && !cell; o = o->getAttachedTo())
	cell = o->getCellProperty();
if (!cell)
	return CellProperty::getWorldCellProperty();
```

- Walks **attach chain** for `CellProperty`; default **world cell**.
- No geometric containment test. Wrong attach parent ⇒ wrong cell with no float threshold.

### 2.6 Passable / closed / disabled (portal state)

| Predicate | Location | Affects dPVS? |
|-----------|----------|---------------|
| `isDisabled()` | `Portal.cpp:322–329` | Yes — NULL target cell (`RenderWorld.cpp:697–700`) |
| `isClosed()` → `ENABLED` | `closedStateChangedHookFunction` `RenderWorld.cpp:754–761` | Yes — portal object disabled in dPVS |
| `isPassable()` / `isPassageAllowed()` | `Portal.cpp:335–368` | **No** for visibility; only `getDestinationCell(passableOnly=true)` |
| `getAccessAllowed()` hook | `CellProperty.cpp:1193–1198` | Gates passability, not dPVS |

