## 3. Camera cell → dPVS handoff (RenderWorld path)

### 3.1 Camera cell assignment (client)

```613:637:src/engine/client/library/clientGame/src/shared/camera/FreeChaseCamera.cpp
const CellProperty* const targetCell = m_target->getParentCell();
if (getParentCell() != targetCell)
	setParentCell(const_cast<CellProperty*>(targetCell));
CellProperty::setPortalTransitionsEnabled(false);
setTransform_o2p(targetObject->getTransform_o2c());
CellProperty::setPortalTransitionsEnabled(true);
// ... then offset, pitch, zoom, collision pull-in ...
```

- **Camera cell = player cell every frame** (forced copy).
- Camera has `addPortalCrossingNotification` (`RenderWorldCamera.cpp:21`) but chase camera **overwrites** cell from target; portal-crossing on camera is **not** authoritative.
- **Split**: `setCell` uses **player’s cell**; `setCameraToCellMatrix` uses **camera’s actual transform** after offset/zoom/collision (`RenderWorld.cpp:888–892`).

### 3.2 Per-frame dPVS setup

```875:893:src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/RenderWorld.cpp
ms_cameraCell = camera.getParentCell();
ms_dpvsCameraCell = ms_cameraCell->getDpvsCell();
...
ms_dpvsCamera->setCell(ms_dpvsCameraCell);
const Transform cameraToCell = camera.getTransform_o2c();
convertToDpvsTransform(cameraToCell, Vector::xyz111, dpvsTransform, camera);
ms_dpvsCamera->setCameraToCellMatrix(dpvsTransform);
```

`getTransform_o2c()` (`Object.cpp:1511–1518`): multiply o2p along attach chain until a `CellProperty` owner is hit.

### 3.3 Visibility resolve

```1093:1093:src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/RenderWorld.cpp
ms_dpvsCamera->resolveVisibility(ms_commander, portalRecusionDepth, 0.0f);
```

- `portalRecusionDepth = 8` (Release `:946`) or 0 if debug `disablePortalTraversal` (`:943`).
- Occlusion bit **off** per evidence (`RenderWorld.cpp:905–931`, cfg default `DOM_off`).

### 3.4 Engine-side portal clipping beyond dPVS

**None for visibility.** `RenderWorldCommander`:

- `QUERY_BEGIN` / `PORTAL_ENTER` / `PORTAL_PRE_EXIT` — pushes/pops **shader sort cell stack** only (`RenderWorldCommander.cpp:211,227–244`).
- `CELL_IMMEDIATE_REPORT` → `RenderWorld::cellVisible` (`:179–185`, `RenderWorld.cpp:1165–1171`) — frame `m_visible` flag; cleared each frame (`clearVisibleCells` `:1079`).

No additional frustum clip of portal quads in engine code.

### 3.5 dPVS object ↔ cell binding

```627:653:src/engine/client/library/clientGraphics/src/shared/RenderWorld.cpp
const CellProperty *cell = object->getParentCell();
dpvsObject->setCell(dpvsCell);
dpvsObject->setObjectToCellMatrix(convertToDpvsTransform(o2c, ...));
```

Interior layout objects added post-zone-in via `ClientInteriorLayoutManager.cpp:153–156` (`addObjectNotifications` + `addToWorld`) — if cell never becomes visible in dPVS that frame, objects exist in graph but **never get `INSTANCE_VISIBLE`**.

---

## 4. dPVS portal predicates (visibility traversal)

### 4.1 Portal visibility pipeline (ordered)

```
isObjectVisible_INTERNAL (dpvsVisibilityQuery_Test.cpp:49)
  → backFaceCull (always for portals, :70–77)
  → setPortalVisible (:308)
      → traversePortal (:512)
          → calculateTransition (ImpPhysicalPortal.cpp:157–171)
          → testTransition / recursion (:616–651)
          → getTestRectangle (:557–558)
          → createFrustumFromRectangle (ImpCamera.cpp:372–423)
```

### 4.2 Portal backface cull — **EPSILON = 0.0f**

```482:519:src/external/3rd/library/dpvs/implementation/sources/dpvsImpMeshModel.cpp
const float EPSILON = 0.0f;
float dist = tlat.x*p.x + tlat.y*p.y + tlat.z*p.z + tlat.w * p.w;
if (dist >= EPSILON) return true;  // front-facing
return false;  // completely back-face culled
```

Portal-specific camera position (`ImpObject.cpp:1829–1838`):

```1829:1838:src/external/3rd/library/dpvs/implementation/sources/dpvsImpObject.cpp
// Portal: camera position in object-space (translation-only, rotation-invariant)
Math::invertMatrix(cellToObject, getObjectToCell());
Math::productFromLeft(tmp, c->getCameraToCell(), cellToObject);
nlat = Vector4(tmp[0][3], tmp[1][3], tmp[2][3], 1.0f);
return m_testModel->backFaceCull(nlat);
```

**Degenerate cases**

| Case | Mechanism | Visual |
|------|-----------|--------|
| Camera **behind** portal plane (`dist < 0`) | BF culled → `traversePortal` fails (`VisibilityQuery_Test.cpp:363–367`) | **Entire interior cell block missing**; world/sky through opening |
| Camera **on** plane (`dist == 0`) | Passes (`>= 0`) | Unstable; float noise can flip sign frame-to-frame → **intermittent** |
| Camera in **player cell** but offset **through doorway** | Cell tag = world, camera position in building space behind entrance plane | Same as behind-plane from world-side portal |
| NaN in transform | `_isnan` FATAL in debug `convertToDpvsTransform` (`RenderWorld.cpp:330–341`); Release FATAL `:346–360` | Would crash, not intermittent silent cull |

### 4.3 Portal screen rectangle + frustum shrink

```557:563:src/external/3rd/library/dpvs/implementation/sources/dpvsVisibilityQuery_Traverse.cpp
if(!p->getTestRectangle(portalRectangle)) return false;
if(!targetCamera->createFrustumFromRectangle(frustum,portalRectangle)) return false;
```

- `getTestRectangle` → `getExactRectangle` for portals (`ImpObject.cpp:1239–1241`).
- `createFrustumFromRectangle`: integer floor/ceil of raster rect, then **intersect** with current viewport (`ImpCamera.cpp:381–390`). Empty intersection → **false**.

**Degenerate cases**

| Case | Visual |
|------|--------|
| Portal projects to **zero-area** or off-screen sliver | Traversal rejected; interior not visited |
| Shallow viewing angle at cantina entrance | Portal hull ≈ line → rectangle collapses; **tiny head turn restores** |
| `importanceThreshold` | Default `0.0f` in resolve call (`RenderWorld.cpp:1093`) → importance gate **disabled** |

### 4.4 Recursion / re-traversal

`testTransition` (`dpvsVisibilityQuery_Traverse.cpp:616–651`): max depth 8, re-traversal block for nested real portals. Unlikely at single building entrance unless mirror/recursive layout.

### 4.5 View-frustum cull on cell contents

After portal accepted, objects in target cell go through standard VF cull (`VIEWFRUSTUM_CULLING` always set in Release `:945–946`). Would not remove **whole cell** at once unless cell never entered.

