## 5. Predicate boundary catalog (summary table)

| ID | Predicate | File:line | Epsilon | Degenerate / boundary | Failure look |
|----|-----------|-----------|---------|----------------------|--------------|
| P1 | Portal plane from winding | `PortalPropertyTemplate.cpp:413–421` | 0 (debug 0.001 coplanar warn) | Degenerate triangle → zero normal | Unpredictable cull / crash in plane setup |
| P2 | Directed plane crossing | `Plane.cpp:242–244` | 0 | On-plane passes; parallel segment fails | Player cell stuck; portal penetration miss |
| P3 | `inPolygon` | `Vector.cpp:253–256` | 0 | Edge/on-vertex | Cell transition miss at doorway |
| P4 | IndexedTriangleList backface | `IndexedTriangleList.cpp:377–378` | `float::min()` | Grazing parallel ray | No penetration detected |
| P5 | `getDestinationCell` closest-t | `CellProperty.cpp:761–764` | 0 | Tie → list order | Wrong adjacent cell (usually not “missing whole cell”) |
| P6 | Portal segment +0.1m lift | `CellProperty.cpp:146–149` | 0.1m fixed | Low portal / terrain seam | Under-portal segment misses |
| P7 | `getParentCell` attach walk | `Object.cpp:1376–1380` | N/A (discrete) | No CellProperty on chain → world | Wrong dPVS root cell |
| P8 | Camera cell = player cell | `FreeChaseCamera.cpp:615–617` | N/A | Player cell wrong → camera cell wrong | Wrong portal graph root |
| P9 | Camera o2c vs cell tag split | `RenderWorld.cpp:888–892` + `FreeChaseCamera.cpp:649–753` | collision t eps 0.25/line | Camera **position** outside tagged cell’s valid half-space | Portal BF cull / wrong frustum origin |
| P10 | dPVS portal BF cull | `ImpMeshModel.cpp:511–516` | **0.0f** | `dist<0` culled; `dist==0` unstable | **Whole cell missing**; sky/wrong wall |
| P11 | dPVS portal rectangle | `VisibilityQuery_Traverse.cpp:557–563` | int snap | Sub-pixel portal projection | Same; **angle-sensitive** |
| P12 | Portal closed/disabled | `RenderWorld.cpp:697–700,754–761` | N/A | Door state | Permanent hole (less likely intermittent) |
| P13 | Interior layout budget | `ClientInteriorLayoutManager.cpp:97–156` | per-frame cap | Objects not yet in world/dPVS | Partial cell content missing post-zone-in |

**No hysteresis** anywhere in render containment path. `CellProperty::m_visible` is per-frame only.

---

## 6. End-to-end: camera containing cell resolution

```
Player moves
  └─ CellProperty::Notification::positionChanged     [CellProperty.cpp:115–185]
       └─ getDestinationCell → testPenetration       [CellProperty.cpp:720–769, Portal.cpp:195–209]
            └─ Object::setParentCell                  [Object.cpp:1387–1408]

FreeChaseCamera::update
  └─ setParentCell(player->getParentCell())          [FreeChaseCamera.cpp:615–617]
  └─ offset / zoom / ClientWorld::collide pull-in    [FreeChaseCamera.cpp:649–753]

RenderWorld::drawScene
  └─ ms_cameraCell = camera.getParentCell()          [RenderWorld.cpp:875]
  └─ dpvsCamera->setCell + setCameraToCellMatrix     [RenderWorld.cpp:888–892]
  └─ resolveVisibility(depth=8)                      [RenderWorld.cpp:1093]
       └─ dPVS portal BF + rectangle + cell traverse
            └─ RenderWorldCommander INSTANCE_*       [RenderWorldCommander.cpp:306–458]
```

**World-cell fallback**: only via `getParentCell()` when attach chain lacks `CellProperty` (`Object.cpp:1379–1380`). Player inside building should attach to cell object (`setParentCell` non-world branch `:1404–1405`).

---

## 7. Rank vs locked facts

Locked symptoms: **(A)** whole cell draw blocks missing, **(B)** tiny camera move restores, **(C)** cantina **entrance** world↔interior, **(D)** gl05+gl11 / Win32+x64, **(E)** clusters post-zone-in, **(F)** occlusion buffer off.

| Rank | Predicate(s) | Consistency rationale |
|------|--------------|----------------------|
| **1** | **P11** dPVS portal screen rectangle + frustum intersect (`VisibilityQuery_Traverse.cpp:557–563`, `ImpCamera.cpp:389–390`) | Explains **42–160 draws** (entire cell subgraph) gone while shared draws unchanged; **classic shallow-angle / sub-pixel portal** sensitivity at doorway; cross-renderer; self-clearing on tiny move; occlusion-independent |
| **2** | **P10** dPVS portal backface cull, **ε=0** (`ImpMeshModel.cpp:511–516`, `ImpObject.cpp:1829–1838`) | Same whole-cell signature; **camera collision offset** (`FreeChaseCamera.cpp:673–753`) can place eye behind entrance plane while cell tag still world; **dist sign flip** on sub-mm move; shared float math; historical FPU neighborhood (2026-06-20 fix) |
| **3** | **P9** camera **cell tag vs actual o2c position** split (`FreeChaseCamera.cpp:615–637` + `RenderWorld.cpp:888–892`) | At entrance, chase cam **outside** player feet; dPVS uses **camera position** for portal tests but **player cell** for root cell — coherent only if entrance portal traversal succeeds; amplifies P10/P11 |
| **4** | **P2–P4, P6** player portal-crossing segment tests (`CellProperty.cpp:115–185`, `IndexedTriangleList.cpp:377–386`) | Wrong **root cell** → wrong portal graph; tiny step changes segment vs portal; **0.1m lift** sensitive at terrain-aligned doors; does not require dPVS bug; intermittent if player “mostly in world” at threshold |
| **5** | **P13** phased interior layout / budgeted preload (`ClientInteriorLayoutManager.cpp`, evidence “post-zone-in”) | Explains **clustering after zone-in** and partial missing draws; weaker on **instant** angle-fix unless combined with P1/P10 race; less pure “whole native cell shell missing” |
| **6** | **P12** closed/disabled portal | Would be stable until door animates; logs show no door errors; lower for intermittent |
| **7** | P5 tie order, P7 attach-chain fallback | Wrong cell usually ≠ entire interior shell vanishing; tie-break rarely entrance-specific |

**Eliminated by evidence**: dPVS occlusion buffer (off), GPU/renderer path (DrawIndexed never emitted), `canSeeParentCell` (loaded in template, **no runtime consumer** in repo).

---

## 8. Decisive experiments (mechanism-only, no fixes)

1. **Instrument** `ms_numberOfPortalsCrossed` (`RenderWorldCommander.cpp:229–230`) on broken vs good frames — 0 crossings with camera facing interior ⇒ P10/P11; wrong cell with 0 crossings ⇒ P4/P7/P8.
2. **Compare** `camera.getParentCell()->isWorldCell()` vs sign of dPVS portal `dist` at entrance portal mesh — tests P9/P10 directly.
3. **Log** `getTestRectangle` failure vs BF cull failure inside dPVS (would require temporary stats hooks in `VisibilityQuery_Traverse.cpp:557–563` and `VisibilityQuery_Test.cpp:73–77`).

---

**Bottom line**: The render submission gate is **`ms_dpvsCamera->resolveVisibility()`** (`RenderWorld.cpp:1093`). Engine portal code supplies geometry and **discrete cell tags**; the geometric predicates that decide **cell-to-cell reachability** for drawing are predominantly **dPVS portal backface (ε=0)** and **portal screen-rectangle/frustum intersection**, fed by a **camera whose cell is copied from the player but whose position is independently collision-adjusted** at the cantina entrance. That combination best matches all locked RenderDoc and behavioral facts.
